# Feature patch 0009 — pattern-fill rasterisation + Type 3 procedural
# vector enumeration. Two unrelated capabilities, five new exports:
#
# Group A — pattern-fill rasterisation (path objects only):
#
#   FPDFRejeb_PathObjGetFillPatternKind(path_obj)
#       → 0 = no pattern (solid colour or no fill), 1 = tiling, 2 = shading.
#       Returns -1 on null / non-path object. Discriminates via the virtual
#       CPDF_Pattern::AsTilingPattern() / AsShadingPattern() accessors —
#       PDFium 7811's CPDF_Pattern has no public GetType() method.
#
#   FPDFRejeb_PathObjGetRenderedBitmap(document, page, path_obj, scale)
#       → FPDF_BITMAP of just this path object, scale-multiplied. Caller
#       owns the bitmap (release with FPDFBitmap_Destroy). Returns NULL on
#       null doc/path, mismatched page document, scale<=0, empty bbox, or
#       allocation failure. Uses the same render-context plumbing pattern
#       upstream uses for FPDFTextObj_GetRenderedBitmap — RenderSingleObject
#       on the path with a flip-and-translate matrix to land it in our
#       throwaway CFX_DefaultRenderDevice. The render context routes through
#       the page resources so pattern dictionaries resolve correctly.
#
#       Why the path layer needs this when text already has it: text
#       glyphs round-trip cleanly through FPDFFont_GetGlyphPath, but path
#       fills with /Pattern resources don't have a vector path equivalent
#       — the pattern's tile (CPDF_TilingPattern) or shading function
#       (CPDF_ShadingPattern) needs the full render pipeline to produce
#       pixels. Single-object rasterise via this export is the escape
#       hatch the downstream renderer uses when it sees PatternKind != 0.
#
# Group B — Type 3 procedural-glyph vector enumeration (text objects only):
#
#   FPDFRejeb_TextObjGetType3CharObjectCount(text_obj, char_index)
#       → number of CPDF_PageObject entries in the Type 3 char's form
#       (== CPDF_Form::GetPageObjectCount()). Returns -1 on null, non-text,
#       non-Type-3 font, sentinel charcode (0xFFFFFFFF), or out-of-range
#       char_index, or if the font has no glyph procedure for the charcode.
#
#   FPDFRejeb_TextObjGetType3CharObjectAt(text_obj, char_index, obj_index)
#       → FPDF_PAGEOBJECT for the obj_index-th page object in the Type 3
#       char's form. Returns NULL on out-of-range, non-Type-3, etc. The
#       returned page object is owned by the font (which is owned by the
#       document) — do NOT call FPDFPageObj_Destroy on it, lifetime is
#       tied to the document.
#
#   FPDFRejeb_TextObjGetType3FontMatrix(text_obj, *out_a..*out_f)
#       → 6 components of CPDF_Type3Font::GetFontMatrix(). Maps per-glyph
#       unit space (typically /FontBBox normalised to 1/1000 units) into
#       the font's text space. Callers that walk the per-char form objects
#       above need to compose this with the text-object matrix to land in
#       page space. Returns false on null / non-text / non-Type-3.
#
#       Why the font matrix is exposed separately rather than baked into
#       the per-char form objects: a Type 3 font is shared across all text
#       objects that reference it, so the form objects are stored in
#       font-local coordinates without per-instance scale. Callers compose
#       (font_matrix * text_matrix) once and apply to every glyph's geometry.
#
# Why bundle Group A + Group B in one patch: both unblock the same
# downstream renderer fallback path (single-object rasterise to FPDF_BITMAP
# when the vector chain can't reproduce upstream's output) and both
# require the same C++ surface — the page-object + render-pipeline
# headers below would otherwise be pulled in by either patch alone.
# Splitting would just duplicate the include churn.
#
# Type 3 form-object access route: CPDF_Type3Char::form() returns a
# CPDF_Font::FormIface*; the patch downcasts to CPDF_Form*, which is the
# only concrete impl AND inherits from CPDF_PageObjectHolder. PDFium 7811's
# CPDF_Form is `final` (core/fpdfapi/page/cpdf_form.h:24) so the
# static_cast is safe — guarded with a header comment so future PDFium
# bumps don't silently regress to UB if a second FormIface impl appears.
#
# Adds two helpers in an unnamed namespace: AsPathObject() (mirrors the
# existing AsTextObject from patch 0008) and GetType3CharForm() (factors
# out the text -> Type3 -> LoadChar -> form chain shared by the two
# Type-3 char-object accessors).
diff --git a/fpdfsdk/fpdf_rejeb.cpp b/fpdfsdk/fpdf_rejeb.cpp
index df86f60..8764a6d 100644
--- a/fpdfsdk/fpdf_rejeb.cpp
+++ b/fpdfsdk/fpdf_rejeb.cpp
